# HTML programs stay inside the machine's limits

The numbers and the full lists live in one place each. Do not copy them here.

- Language, Canvas and size limits:
  [docs/JMR_JS_COMPATIBILITY.md](../../docs/JMR_JS_COMPATIBILITY.md)
  ([Limits](../../docs/JMR_JS_COMPATIBILITY.md#limits),
  [Names the compiler rejects](../../docs/JMR_JS_COMPATIBILITY.md#names-the-compiler-rejects)).
- How to write a program (art, text, input, sound, speed, memory):
  [docs/GAME_DESIGN.md](../../docs/GAME_DESIGN.md).
- Menus, windows, dialogs, files:
  [docs/SYSTEM_APPLICATIONS.md](../../docs/SYSTEM_APPLICATIONS.md).
- Words: [docs/WORDS.md](../../docs/WORDS.md#words-used-in-this-project).

## Rules

- A page that runs in Chrome is not proof. Check every new or changed program
  with `python3 tools/check_port.py storage/NAME.HTML`, then run it in the
  Python model and FPGA-SIM. A program that fails to compile gets no `.JSH`
  and will not start.
- Programs start from Finder (double-click). The card builder compiles every
  program in `storage/`; on the machine, Finder's Special → Compile does the
  same job. Do not add a second compile path.
- When a program hits a limit, change the program: pack frames into at most
  16 art sheets, split a function that needs more than 16 parameters plus
  locals, use row arrays for a map larger than 128 elements, reuse objects
  instead of allocating every frame. Do not cut game content to fit, and do
  not raise a machine limit for one title.
- Never gate behaviour on a program's name (`if (stem == "…")`).
  [no-game-hardwire.mdc](no-game-hardwire.mdc).
- `img.src = "jmr:spr:N"` must be a string literal per sheet.
- Text is one 8×8 bitmap font, ASCII 32–126. Do not add fonts to the RTL.
- Esc leaves the program. Do not bind it.
- No per-frame maze flood or other unbounded per-tick work.
  [no-maze-flood-on-tick.mdc](no-maze-flood-on-tick.mdc).
- Do not delete the system programs in `storage/`: `FINDER`, `EDITOR`, `READ`,
  `NOTE`, `UTILITY`, `COMPILE`, `ARTSCAN`, `COMPILER`, `COMPIL2`.
